# DMM v1 stage A (breadboard): Arduino Mega + ADS124S08 (TQFP-32 on an adapter board) + SSD1306 OLED module.
# J3 is the bundle of jumper wires to the Mega (the Mega itself is not drawn).
# IOVDD = 5 V so the Mega's 5 V SPI connects directly (datasheet: IOVDD DVDD..5.25 V, DVDD 2.7..3.6 V).
# Single ground for now (AVSS = DGND = Mega GND); AVDD is the Mega 5 V through an RC filter.
# Build: ccad dmm/stageA.ccad   (Pico version: stageA_pico.ccad)
new
add ADS124S08_TQFP as=U1
add HEADER12 as=J3
add HEADER4 as=J1
add HEADER6 as=J2
add R 10 as=R1
add C 10u as=C1
add C 100n as=C2
add C 100n as=C3
add C 100n as=C4
add C 1u as=C5
add ADR4525 as=U2
add C 100n as=C6
add C 1u as=C7
add C 1u as=C8

# Supplies from the Mega: 5 V for I/O (and AVDD through R1 / C1 / C2), 3.3 V for the digital core
net 5V J3.1 U1.IOVDD C3.1 R1.1 J1.2 U2.VIN C6.1 C7.1
net AVDD R1.2 U1.AVDD C1.1 C2.1
net 3V3 J3.2 U1.DVDD C4.1
net GND J3.3 U1.AVSS U1.AVSS-SW U1.DGND U1.REFCOM U1.CLK C1.2 C2.2 C3.2 C4.2 C5.2 J1.1 J2.6 U2.GND C6.2 C7.2 C8.2 U1.REFN0 U1.AINCOM

# Internal 2.5 V reference: REFOUT needs 1 uF to REFCOM. Also on AIN5 for the comparison below.
net REFOUT U1.REFOUT C5.1 J2.1 U1.AIN5

# Second, independent 2.5 V reference (ADR4525: VIN 3..15 V, COUT >= 1 uF, pin 8 TP left open).
# On AIN4 and on REFP0 (REFN0 to AVSS), so the two references can be compared both ways:
#   AIN4 - AIN5 at high PGA gain gives the difference of the two directly (a few mV),
#   and REFP0 lets the ADR4525 be the ADC reference instead of the internal one.
net ADRREF U2.VOUT C8.1 U1.AIN4 U1.REFP0

# SPI of the Mega (D50-D53) and control lines (D2 = INT4 for DRDY)
net MISO U1.DOUT/DRDY J3.4
net MOSI U1.DIN J3.5
net SCLK U1.SCLK J3.6
net CS U1.CS J3.7
net DRDY U1.DRDY J3.8
net START U1.START/SYNC J3.9
net RESET U1.RESET J3.10

# I2C of the Mega (D20 SDA, D21 SCL) to the OLED module
net SDA J3.11 J1.4
net SCL J3.12 J1.3

# Analog test inputs
net AIN0 U1.AIN0 J2.2
net AIN1 U1.AIN1 J2.3
net AIN2 U1.AIN2 J2.4
net AIN3 U1.AIN3 J2.5

# AINCOM is tied to GND so single-ended inputs can be measured against it (AINx - AINCOM).
# Unused ADC inputs float (datasheet 10.1.5: lowest leakage); GPIOs stay analog inputs
nc U1.REFP1/AIN6 U1.REFN1/AIN7 U1.GPIO0/AIN8 U1.GPIO1/AIN9 U1.GPIO2/AIN10 U1.GPIO3/AIN11 U1.NC
nc U2.TP

pinnames J1 GND,VCC,SCL,SDA
pinnames J2 REFOUT,AIN0,AIN1,AIN2,AIN3,GND
pinnames J3 5V,3V3,GND,D50,D51,D52,D53,D2,D4,D5,D20,D21
erc
save dmm/stageA.schjson
